%description:

The standard deviation of the shadow fading of an indoor UE's link, as TR 36.873
and TR 38.901 give it: 7 dB in UMa (and UMi), 8 dB in RMa.
ChannelModelIndoorShadowing has the outdoor UE's link, which keeps the sigma of
its LOS state.

TR 36.873 v12.7.0 7.2.3, rows "3D-UMi O2I" and "3D-UMa O2I": "sigma_SF =7"; the
O2I columns of Table 7.3-6 have the same in "Shadow fading (SF) [dB]".
TR 38.901 v16.1.0 Table 7.5-6 ("Channel model parameters"), row "Shadow fading
(SF) [dB]", sigma_SF: Part-1, UMi - Street Canyon and UMa, O2I: "7"; Part-2,
RMa, O2I: "8" (LOS and NLOS: "See Table 7.4.1-1", which has no O2I value).
Table 7.4.3-3, the single-frequency model below 6 GHz, gives the same 7 dB:
"7 dB (note: replacing the respective value in Table 7.4.1-1)".

Checked on the first shadowing value of eight indoor UEs' links, in LOS and in
NLOS: under TR 38.901 on a UMa cell at 2 GHz and at 28 GHz and on an RMa cell
at 2 GHz, and under TR 36.873 on a UMa cell at 2 GHz. The harness has both
carriers, so TR 38.901's values are those of Table 7.5-6. The value is one
N(0, sigma) draw; it is divided by the standard-normal draw replayed from a
copy of the model's generator, which gives sigma. The cases are graded
against t901_sigma_o2i_uma, t901_sigma_o2i_rma and t873_sigma_o2i of
pathloss_reference.py.

%includes:
#include "SchedulerTestUtil.h"
#include "ChannelModelTestUtil.h"
#include "PathLossTestUtil.h"

%global:
using namespace simu5g;
using namespace simu5g::unittest;
using inet::Coord;

%file: harness.ned
import simu5g.common.binder.Binder;
import simu5g.stack.phy.medium.CellularRadioMedium;
import simu5g.common.carrierAggregation.CarrierAggregation;
import simu5g.stack.phy.channelmodel.Tr36873ChannelModel;
import simu5g.stack.phy.channelmodel.Tr38901ChannelModel;

network Harness
{
    submodules:
        binder: Binder;
        radioMedium: CellularRadioMedium;
        carrierAggregation: CarrierAggregation;
        model901: Tr38901ChannelModel;
        model901mm: Tr38901ChannelModel {
            componentCarrierModule = "carrierAggregation.componentCarrier[1]";
        }
        model873: Tr36873ChannelModel;
        test: Test;
}

%inifile: omnetpp.ini
[General]
network = Harness
cmdenv-express-mode = false
cmdenv-log-prefix = ""
sim-time-limit = 1s

# one carrier below 6 GHz and one above
*.carrierAggregation.numComponentCarriers = 2
*.carrierAggregation.componentCarrier[0].carrierFrequency = 2GHz
*.carrierAggregation.componentCarrier[0].numBands = 10
*.carrierAggregation.componentCarrier[1].carrierFrequency = 28GHz
*.carrierAggregation.componentCarrier[1].numBands = 10
**.cellInfoModule = ""
*.binder.printTrafficGeneratorConfig = false

**.shadowing = true
**.fading = false
**.dynamicLos = false
**.fixedLos = true

%no-default-inifile: 1

%activity:
auto *model901 = harnessModule<StochasticChannelModel>(this, "model901");
auto *model901mm = harnessModule<StochasticChannelModel>(this, "model901mm");
auto *model873 = harnessModule<StochasticChannelModel>(this, "model873");
auto *medium = harnessModule<CellularRadioMedium>(this, "radioMedium");

// a UMa and an RMa base station, and UEs at one place, 100 m from them: a link
// each, so a first shadowing value each
StubEndpoint bsEndpoint;
bsEndpoint.nodeId = MacNodeId(1);
bsEndpoint.coord = Coord(0, 0, 25);
StubRadioRegistration bsRadio(medium, bsEndpoint.nodeId, &bsEndpoint);
StubEndpoint rmaEndpoint;
rmaEndpoint.nodeId = MacNodeId(2);
rmaEndpoint.scenario = RURAL_MACROCELL;
rmaEndpoint.coord = Coord(0, 0, 35);
StubRadioRegistration rmaRadio(medium, rmaEndpoint.nodeId, &rmaEndpoint);
StubEndpoint ues[8];
std::vector<std::unique_ptr<StubRadioRegistration>> ueRadios;
for (int i = 0; i < 8; i++) {
    ues[i].nodeId = MacNodeId(1025 + i);
    ues[i].coord = Coord(100, 0, 1.5);
    ueRadios.push_back(std::make_unique<StubRadioRegistration>(medium, ues[i].nodeId, &ues[i]));
}

wait(0.010);

// The standard deviation a link's first shadowing value was drawn with: the
// value is one N(0, sigma) draw, replayed here as a standard-normal one from a
// copy of the model's generator, so their ratio is sigma.
auto sigmaOf = [&] (StochasticChannelModel *model, StubEndpoint& bs, StubEndpoint& ue, bool indoor, bool los) {
    ue.insideBuilding = indoor;
    ue.insideDistance = indoor ? 10.0 : 0.0;
    double d2D = 100.0, d3D = std::sqrt(100.0 * 100.0 + (bs.coord.z - 1.5) * (bs.coord.z - 1.5));
    ChannelModelProbe probe(model);
    RadioLink link = probe.whatIfLink(&ue, dlCqiTransmission(&bs, ue.nodeId));
    RngSnapshot snapshot(model);
    double value = model->computeShadowing(d3D, d2D, los, link);
    return value / omnetpp::normal(snapshot.rng(), 0, 1);
};

CaseRecorder probe(this, 1e-9);
probe.record("t901_sigma_o2i_uma", {}, sigmaOf(model901, bsEndpoint, ues[0], true, true));
probe.record("t901_sigma_o2i_uma", {}, sigmaOf(model901, bsEndpoint, ues[1], true, false));
probe.record("t901_sigma_o2i_uma", {}, sigmaOf(model901mm, bsEndpoint, ues[2], true, true));
probe.record("t901_sigma_o2i_uma", {}, sigmaOf(model901mm, bsEndpoint, ues[3], true, false));
probe.record("t901_sigma_o2i_rma", {}, sigmaOf(model901, rmaEndpoint, ues[4], true, true));
probe.record("t901_sigma_o2i_rma", {}, sigmaOf(model901, rmaEndpoint, ues[5], true, false));
probe.record("t873_sigma_o2i", {}, sigmaOf(model873, bsEndpoint, ues[6], true, true));
probe.record("t873_sigma_o2i", {}, sigmaOf(model873, bsEndpoint, ues[7], true, false));

%postrun-command: ../../pathloss_reference.py --grade test.out >verdict.txt

%contains: verdict.txt
graded=8 failures=0

%not-contains: verdict.txt
FAILED

%not-contains: stdout
FAILED
